<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
	<dict>
		<!--
			MSAL on iOS always uses iOSTokenCacheAccessor (iOSPlatformProxy.CreateTokenCacheAccessor
			returns it unconditionally - WithCacheOptions cannot opt out). Its constructor calls
			GetTeamId(), which writes a probe item to the keychain and reads back its access group;
			with no keychain-access-groups entitlement that fails and every PublicClientApplication
			build throws MsalClientException(cannot_access_publisher_keychain). That failed all 10
			Given_MsalAuthentication cases on the simulator lane in build 228812.

			MSAL then uses "<first dot component of the access group>.com.microsoft.adalcache" as its
			keychain group, so the entitled group has to be exactly that. A shipping app writes
			"$(AppIdentifierPrefix)com.microsoft.adalcache" and gets the prefix from its provisioning
			profile; this head is a CI test app that is never signed with a team, and the simulator
			does not validate the group against a profile, so a synthetic prefix works and keeps the
			build free of signing configuration.
		-->
		<key>keychain-access-groups</key>
		<array>
			<string>unoexttests.com.microsoft.adalcache</string>
		</array>
	</dict>
</plist>
